Coca-Cola says its business is built around a broad portfolio of branded beverages, sold through both concentrate operations and finished-product operations, and distributed worldwide through bottlers, distributors, wholesalers, retailers, and its own bottling operations. It says beverages bearing its owned or licensed trademarks account for “2.2 billion” of the estimated 65 billion servings consumed worldwide each day. [KO · FY2025 · business/mda · 0001628280-26-010047]

On brands and beverage categories, the 10-K says it owns and markets numerous beverage brands across several groups, including:  
- sparkling soft drinks: Coca-Cola, Diet Coke/Coca-Cola Light, Coca-Cola Zero Sugar, Fanta, Fresca, Schweppes, Sprite, and Thums Up;  
- water, sports, coffee and tea: Aquarius, Ayataka, BODYARMOR, Ciel, Costa, Crystal, Dasani, Fuze Tea, Georgia, glacéau smartwater, glacéau vitaminwater, Gold Peak, I LOHAS, Powerade, and Topo Chico;  
- juice, value-added dairy and plant-based beverages: Core Power, Del Valle, fairlife, innocent, Maaza, Minute Maid, Minute Maid Pulpy, Santa Clara, and Simply. [KO · FY2025 · business · 0001628280-26-010047]

